Transcript of Cell
The cell has different little organs named organells that realize specific functions like the organs of our body.
The cell is considered the smallest living being because it realize all the individual functions.
It is located near of the centre of the cell, it is surrounded by a membrane and controlls every task of the cell.
It is located inside of the Nucleous and contains RNA and DNA (genetic information)
It contains the organelles, it is outside of the nucleus but inside of themembrane.
They are a storage for minerals,food and waste, they also have different shapes in animal and plant cells ( they are large in plant cells and smaller in animal cells)
They help in the making of proteines, they can be founded in the cytoplasm.
It is the connection between the cell membrane and the nuclear membrane, it also allow the materials of the cell to move across the whole cell.
They are tiny sacks that store proteines.
They are the ones that have the enzymes used for digestio, if one of them burst, it can destroy the cell.
It is used for respiration, they relase the energy of the cells.
The plant Cells have specific parts:
-Cell Wall: protects and supports the cell.
-Chloro Plasts: gives the green pigment that is named chlorophyll.
ChromoPlasts: gives the pigment to the flowers.
The animal cells don't present the cell wall, or the chloro plast and chromo plast but they present the centrioles that help the cell with the mitosis.

